    <bpmn:process id="W_W1832" name="W1832. Private Label Product Specification &amp; Sample Development" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Factory qualified (W1831) and product scope defined (W1830)
Frequency: ~20–30 new private label SKU specifications/year
Volume: Average 8–15 SKUs per product development initiative
Owner: Category Manager
Participants: Category Manager, Buyer, Quality Assurance Manager, Packaging Designer, Merchandise Planner
Source: workflow W1832 — Private Label Product Specification &amp; Sample Development</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1832_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1832_Lane1" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1832_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1832_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1832_Lane2" name="Buyer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1832_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1832_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1832_Lane3" name="Quality Assurance Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1832_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1832_Lane4" name="Packaging Designer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1832_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1832_Lane5" name="Merchandise Planner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1832_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1832_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1832_Start7" name="Factory qualified (W1831) and product scope defined (W1830)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1832_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1832_Task8" name="Category Manager develops detailed product specification for each SKU: (a)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Category Manager develops detailed product specification for each SKU: (a) product description and intended use, (b) material composition and grade (e.g., &quot;carbon steel Grade 8.8&quot; for bolts, &quot;304 stainless steel&quot; for screws, &quot;polypropylene woven 120 GSM&quot; for tarps), (c) dimensional specifications with tolerances (length, width, thickness, weight), (d) performance requirements (tensile strength, corrosion resistance, impact resistance, load capacity — per product type), (e) color and finish requirements, (f) packaging specifications: unit pack quantity, display box quantity, master carton quantity, barcoding (EAN-13 or UPC-A), (g) labeling requirements: product name, BuildRight logo, country of origin, material composition, size, quantity, usage instructions, safety warnings per Philippine labeling regulations (Consumer Act RA 7394), DTI-BPS requirements, (h) shelf life requirements (if applicable — adhesives, chemicals, paint accessories), (i) quality control checkpoints: what must be inspected at factory, at incoming receipt, and at store
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1–2 hours/SKU</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1832_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1832_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1832_Task9" name="Buyer transmits specification to qualified factory; factory produces first…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Buyer transmits specification to qualified factory; factory produces first article samples (FAS): (a) factory produces 3–5 units per SKU per specification, (b) factory provides specification conformance report documenting materials, dimensions, and test results, (c) factory ships samples to BuildRight HQ for evaluation
Responsible (R): Buyer
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2–4 weeks (factory production + shipping)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1832_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1832_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1832_Task10" name="Quality Assurance Manager conducts first article inspection (FAI): (a)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Quality Assurance Manager conducts first article inspection (FAI): (a) dimensional verification: measure all critical dimensions against specification tolerances using calibrated instruments, (b) material verification: confirm material composition matches specification (may require lab testing — tensile test, hardness test, salt spray test for corrosion resistance), (c) functional testing: test product in intended application (e.g., drive screws into wood, test paint roller nap absorption, test tarp waterproofing), (d) packaging and labeling verification: confirm packaging meets specification, barcodes scan correctly, labels comply with Philippine regulations, (e) document FAI results: pass/fail per specification parameter; if fail, document specific non-conformances and required corrective actions
Responsible (R): Quality Assurance Manager
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours/SKU</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1832_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1832_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1832_Task11" name="If FAI fails: Buyer communicates non-conformances to factory; factory produces…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: If FAI fails: Buyer communicates non-conformances to factory; factory produces revised samples; repeat step 2–3. Maximum 3 sample rounds before escalating to Category Manager for factory re-evaluation (W1831.5 fallback factory). Typical: 1–2 sample rounds for experienced factories; 2–3 rounds for new factories.
Responsible (R): Buyer / Quality Assurance Manager
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2–4 weeks per sample round</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1832_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1832_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1832_Task12" name="Packaging Designer develops packaging artwork for approved products: (a) brand…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Packaging Designer develops packaging artwork for approved products: (a) brand identity: &quot;BuildRight Essentials&quot; or &quot;BuildRight Pro&quot; logo placement per brand guidelines, (b) product photography or illustration, (c) bilingual labeling (English and Filipino per DTI requirement), (d) barcode placement and print quality specification (GS1 standards), (e) color-coded category identification (e.g., blue for hardware, green for garden, orange for PPE), (f) sustainability messaging if applicable (recycled materials, recyclable packaging)
Responsible (R): Packaging Designer
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 1–2 days/SKU batch</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1832_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1832_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1832_Task13" name="Merchandise Planner creates SKU in item master: (a) item type = &quot;Standard Stock…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Merchandise Planner creates SKU in item master: (a) item type = &quot;Standard Stock — Private Label&quot;, (b) brand field = &quot;BuildRight Essentials&quot; or &quot;BuildRight Pro&quot;, (c) product specifications linked to SKU record, (d) reorder parameters set per W2A (ROP, safety stock, EOQ), (e) pricing populated per W1833 (cost modeling output), (f) product content populated for ecommerce listing per W316 (digital asset master)
Responsible (R): Merchandise Planner
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 15 min/SKU</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1832_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1832_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1832_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1832_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1832_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-173 (prevent non-compliant private-label products from reaching shelf.) | - operational: Category Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Category Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1832_Assoc16" sourceRef="W1832_Annotation15" targetRef="W1832_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
