    <bpmn:process id="W_W1837" name="W1837. Private Label Supplier Contract Renewal, Renegotiation &amp; Transition Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Factory contract expiration (typically 1–2 year terms); performance decline triggering supplier change
Frequency: ~8–12 contract renewals/year; ~1–2 supplier transitions/year
Volume: ~15–25 active private label factory contracts at any time
Owner: Buyer
Participants: Buyer, Category Manager, Quality Assurance Manager, FP&amp;A, VP Merchandising
Source: workflow W1837 — Private Label Supplier Contract Renewal, Renegotiation &amp; Transition Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1837_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1837_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1837_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1837_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1837_Lane2" name="Buyer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1837_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1837_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1837_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1837_Lane3" name="FP&amp;A">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1837_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1837_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1837_Start5" name="Factory contract expiration (typically 1–2 year terms); performance decline triggering…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1837_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1837_Task6" name="System alerts Buyer 90 days before contract expiry with performance summary…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: System alerts Buyer 90 days before contract expiry with performance summary: (a) on-time delivery rate, (b) quality rejection rate, (c) price competitiveness vs. market benchmarks, (d) responsiveness and communication score, (e) total spend volume
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Buyer
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1837_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1837_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1837_Task7" name="Renew at existing terms">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Buyer evaluates renewal options: (a) Renew at existing terms: factory performing well (scorecard ≥ 85%), pricing competitive, no supply risk — recommend renewal, (b) Renegotiate: factory performing adequately (scorecard 70–85%) but pricing has drifted above market or quality needs improvement — negotiate improved terms (price reduction, quality improvement plan, better payment terms), (c) Transition to new factory: factory underperforming (scorecard &lt; 70%), quality issues unresolved, or pricing uncompetitive — initiate W1831 sourcing for replacement factory, (d) Dual-source: add second factory to reduce supply risk for critical categories
Responsible (R): Buyer
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2–4 hours/contract</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1837_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1837_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1837_Task8" name="For renegotiation: Buyer negotiates with factory using performance data and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: For renegotiation: Buyer negotiates with factory using performance data and market benchmarks: (a) price adjustment request based on landed cost model update (W1833), (b) quality improvement commitment with measurable targets, (c) delivery performance improvement plan, (d) updated MOQ and payment terms, (e) if factory agrees: update contract in system with revised terms, (f) if factory refuses reasonable terms: proceed to transition (step 4)
Responsible (R): Buyer
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1837_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1837_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1837_Task9" name="For transition to new factory: (a) initiate W1831 sourcing for replacement…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: For transition to new factory: (a) initiate W1831 sourcing for replacement factory — allow 3–4 months for sourcing, sample development, and qualification, (b) place final order with current factory to cover inventory during transition period (typically 3–6 months of supply), (c) once new factory qualified: place initial order per W1834, (d) upon first receipt from new factory: conduct heightened quality inspection per W1834.4, (e) if new factory quality acceptable: discontinue orders from old factory; let existing inventory sell through, (f) if new factory quality fails: continue with old factory under revised terms while sourcing second alternative
Responsible (R): Buyer / Quality Assurance Manager
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 3–6 months</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1837_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1837_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1837_Task10" name="FP&amp;A tracks transition cost: (a) dual-sourcing period inventory carrying cost…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: FP&amp;A tracks transition cost: (a) dual-sourcing period inventory carrying cost, (b) new factory qualification cost (samples, testing, travel), (c) any transition pricing differential, (d) report transition ROI to Category Manager and VP Merchandising
Responsible (R): FP&amp;A
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: Monthly during transition</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1837_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1837_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1837_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1837_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1837_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-364 (ensure controlled execution — Private Label Product Development &amp; Sourcing (PA-41.1).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: Buyer</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
